depends on how you want it to work. if you copy the entire thing and paste it again, but change the ID, itll work, but itll do a separate roll for both states. you can end up only extending one state, but not the other.
if you want it to be all or nothing, you can add braces to the conditional statement and an extra line for each state.
Code:
if (Math.random() <.5){
  target.setStateTurns(x, target.stateTurns(x)+1);
  target.setStateTurns(y, target.stateTurns(y)+1);
}

